[...]
>       register int area = (sroom->hx - sroom->lx) * (sroom->hy - sroom->ly);
>       return( area > 20 );

     Looks like off-by-one error (squared :-) to me.  If the hx/ly fields
represent the inside region of the room, 3x9 will result in 16 instead of 27
using that calculation.  A shop with 27 wands would actually need to be
either 4x9 or 3x10; the former would be caught by even the buggy area check
(24), but the latter would slip through (18).

